atlas learning
# Harvested run6/run7 learning/promotion path (Aurekai): the recursive loop that
# learns how the graph itself should evolve. Registered architectural until built.

architecture pattern-graph
  canonical_name PatternGraph
  family learning
  domain Learning / Patterns
  layer learning
  semantic_question What recurring pattern do these action traces and residuals cluster into?
  purpose Action traces -> residuals -> pattern clusters, the raw material of promotion. Above Bonfyre's operation, Aurekai's learning.
  maturity architectural
  node_types ActionTrace
  node_types PatternCluster
  edge_types clusters_into
  forbidden_inference a pattern observed -> a validated primitive
  source_lineage run6/run7 Aurekai learning path
  known_gap not built; the route-ranker learns route ordering, a first learned organ

architecture capability-genome
  canonical_name CapabilityGenome
  family learning
  domain Learning / Promotion
  layer learning
  semantic_question What structural change to the graph does this pattern justify, and has it been proven?
  purpose Pattern cluster -> LambdaTensor motif -> CapabilityGenome -> candidate primitive -> proof -> promotion into the registry. The learned router may improve constantly without mutating constitutional state.
  maturity architectural
  node_types LambdaTensor
  node_types CandidatePrimitive
  edge_types promotes_to
  forbidden_inference a learned candidate -> a promoted primitive (proof and validation gate promotion)
  interacts proof-frontier
  interacts route-ranker
  source_lineage run6/run7 Aurekai learning path
  known_gap not built
